# Who may talk to the instance metadata API. spe-internet loads this table in
# both modes, so it holds whether the internet is on or off.
#
# The metadata API is HTTP on port 80 at 169.254.169.254. It hands out this
# instance's identity and, if a cloud role is attached, its credentials. Only
# two local identities need it:
#   root       the boot-time spe-identity step and the cloud guest agents
#   terraform  the administrator
# Everyone else, the researcher included, is refused immediately.
#
# Only port 80 is restricted. On GCP the same address is also the VM's DNS
# resolver (udp/tcp 53) and NTP server (udp 123); those are not the metadata
# API and are governed by the internet mode instead, not by this table.
#
# Only the opening packet of a connection, the SYN, is judged. It is the one
# packet that always belongs to a live socket with an owner. Once a program has
# closed its socket the kernel still answers the other side on its behalf, and
# those FIN and ACK replies have no owner to check; refusing them left the
# metadata server retransmitting to closed ports for minutes and filled Zeek's
# log with those retries.
table inet spe_metadata {
    chain output {
        type filter hook output priority filter - 10; policy accept;

        ip daddr 169.254.169.254 tcp dport 80 tcp flags syn / syn,ack meta skuid { root, terraform } counter accept
        ip daddr 169.254.169.254 tcp dport 80 tcp flags syn / syn,ack counter reject
    }
}
